<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tlos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tlos was one of the oldest and largest cities of ancient Lycia, on a hill above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xanthos">Xanthos</a> valley in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, generally identified with the Dalawa of Hittite texts. It was one of the six leading members of the Lycian League. Its acropolis is cut with rock tombs, including one with a relief of the hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellerophon">Bellerophon</a> on Pegasus, and an Ottoman fortress later crowned the hill.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tlos.jpg" alt="Tlos" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dosseman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tlos_Stadium_4152.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
